# C# guidance

- Follow `.editorconfig`, the existing project structure, and the applicable
  feature plan.
- Check the relevant project file and `global.json` before relying on a
  framework or language feature.
- Preserve the boundaries described in `.specify/memory/constitution.md`;
  avoid introducing new architectural layers without a concrete requirement.
- Keep I/O asynchronous and propagate cancellation where the surrounding API
  supports it.
- Add or update tests for changed behaviour, following nearby test patterns.
- Run the relevant checks from `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
